Because their heart really isn't in it.  Conflict means monsters
take swings at anything adjacent to them.  While a player will
keep hitting the same monster until it dies, conflict will cause
monsters to hit any adjacent monster without focusing on one
until it dies.  So the crowd will start out thinly quickly just because
so many monsters are hitting each other, but the feweer are left
the fewer are hitting each other.  In the end it tapers off to being
slower than if a player were trying to clean out the level.

But once Rodney and the Dark One face off, they will spend as
much effort trying to steal the Amulet from each other as they
will in combat.  The one not holding the Amulet will steal, the
one holding the Amulet will heal and hit.  It doesn't quite work
out to form a stable system where neither will ever kill the other
but it will sure be a lot slower than if you went in and whacked
until you could pick up the Amulet off the corpse.



